-- title:
--   Recognition of the quadruple at an odd vertex
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $\kappa$ a field of characteristic $p$ equipped with a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-algebra structure; let $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_p)$ have underlying matrix $\mathrm{diag}(p,1)$, let $c' \in \kappa$ satisfy $c'^p \neq c'$, and let $d$ be a Deligne datum over $\kappa$ for the uniformiser $p \in \mathbb{Z}_p$ of $\mathbb{Q}_p$ (an assignment, to each full $\mathbb{Z}_p$-lattice $M$ in $\mathbb{Q}_p^2$, of a submodule $d.\mathrm{line}(M)$ of $\kappa \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_p} M$ with invertible quotient, monotone, homothety-equivariant and nondegenerate at every prime). Assume that the line of $d$ at the lattice $g\,\mathbb{Z}_p^2$ is the image, under the base-changed action isomorphism `actBaseChange` of $g$, of the $\kappa$-span of $1 \otimes e_0 + c' \otimes e_1$, where $e_0, e_1$ is the standard basis of $\mathbb{Z}_p^2$. Let $Q$ be a Drinfeld datum over $\kappa$ for the same uniformiser, and let $x$ be a prime of $\kappa$. Then `Q.IsQuadrupleOf d` — that at every prime $y$ of $\kappa$ the pair $(Q.L_0(y), Q.L_1(y))$ is edge-nondegenerate for $d$ and the kernels of $u_{0,y}$, $u_{1,y}$ are the lines of the datum $d$ base-changed to the local ring at $y$ — holds if and only if there are equalities $h_0 : Q.N_0(x) = p^{-1} g\,\mathbb{Z}_p^2$ and $h_1 : Q.N_1(x) = p^{-1} g\,\mathbb{Z}_p^2$ (the lattice obtained from $g\,\mathbb{Z}_p^2$ by the action of the scalar matrix attached to the inverse of the unit $p$ of $\mathbb{Q}_p$) such that the kernels of $u_0(x)$ and of $u_1(x)$ are each the free rank-one submodule, over the local ring of $\kappa$ at $x$, generated by the vector $1 \otimes e_0 + c' \otimes e_1$ carried successively by the base-changed action isomorphisms of $g$ and of the scalar $p^{-1}$ and then transported along $h_0$, respectively $h_1$.
--
--   This is a recognition statement in the Čerednik–Drinfeld theory: it identifies exactly which Drinfeld quadruples over a field of characteristic $p$ arise from the point of the formal upper half-plane lying in the interior of the odd vertex $[g\,\mathbb{Z}_p^2]$ of the standard edge chart, namely those with $N_0 = N_1 = \mathbb{Z}_p \oplus p^{-1}\mathbb{Z}_p$ and both stalk kernels equal to the transported chart line. It is used in the construction of Cartier quadruples along an edge isogeny, in [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_isCartierQuadruple_map_line_eq_of_edge_isogeny_of_apply_xi_eq_zero_of_apply_eta_ne_zero`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_isCartierQuadruple_map_line_eq_of_edge_isogeny_of_apply_xi_eq_zero_of_apply_eta_ne_zero).
